1
00:00:01,586 --> 00:00:05,382
Phew! Wow. It is raining
cats and dogs out there.

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,217
Holy moly!

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:10,553
Phyllis says the same 12
clichÃ©s every time it rains.

4
00:00:10,637 --> 00:00:14,557
So, I promised everyone that if
she says them all by noon today,

5
00:00:14,641 --> 00:00:17,102
I will send out
for hot chocolates.

6
00:00:17,477 --> 00:00:18,603
So how was the drive in?

7
00:00:18,728 --> 00:00:20,522
Nobody knows how to
drive in the rain.

8
00:00:20,605 --> 00:00:21,940
You don't say?
Yeah.

9
00:00:22,065 --> 00:00:25,443
You know the roads are actually the
slickest in the first half hour?

10
00:00:26,903 --> 00:00:29,989
- I think it's the oil, it comes to the surface.
- I agree.

11
00:00:30,949 --> 00:00:34,536
Ooh! The plants are gonna love this.
Yeah.

12
00:00:39,666 --> 00:00:42,043
I actually sleep
better when it's raining.

13
00:00:42,127 --> 00:00:43,294
Tell me about it.

14
00:00:43,712 --> 00:00:46,381
Time's almost up. How many are left?
Just one.

15
00:00:46,464 --> 00:00:49,467
"This weather makes me want to stay
at home, curled up with a good book."

16
00:00:51,302 --> 00:00:55,098
Phyllis, this rain, does it make
you want to be doing something?

17
00:00:55,306 --> 00:00:56,766
What do you mean?

18
00:00:56,850 --> 00:01:00,353
You know, like, aren't some things
just so nice and cozy in the rain?

19
00:01:00,437 --> 00:01:03,022
Hey, come on. Lots of things
are cozy in the rain.

20
00:01:04,649 --> 00:01:06,735
And that's noon.
Exactly!

21
00:01:07,819 --> 00:01:09,571
Sorry about that,
everybody.

22
00:01:10,822 --> 00:01:12,949
Hey, Phyllis, would you
like a hot chocolate?

23
00:01:13,032 --> 00:01:14,075
Ooh, I'd love one.

24
00:01:14,159 --> 00:01:16,661
I'm going out to get
two hot chocolates.

25
00:01:20,915 --> 00:01:23,209
I mean, normally the rain would
make me want to stay at home,

26
00:01:23,293 --> 00:01:24,627
curled up with
a good book,

27
00:01:24,711 --> 00:01:27,213
but everybody's being
so nice to me today.

28
00:01:27,297 --> 00:01:28,840
I'm really happy
being here.

29
00:01:53,656 --> 00:01:56,951
My girlfriend's back and
there's going to be trouble

30
00:01:57,035 --> 00:01:58,745
Hey, Ia, hey, Ia,
his girlfriend's back

31
00:01:58,828 --> 00:02:00,789
Hey, Ia, hey, Ia,
my girlfriend's back

32
00:02:02,081 --> 00:02:04,000
A month ago, I walked
out of this office

33
00:02:04,083 --> 00:02:05,835
positive I was
never coming back.

34
00:02:07,378 --> 00:02:08,797
I probably shouldn't
have emailed everyone

35
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,965
telling them exactly
what I thought of them.

36
00:02:11,216 --> 00:02:13,092
Hey, Erin, thank you
for the nice email.

37
00:02:13,968 --> 00:02:17,096
Yeah. I don't get emotional
a lot, but that was...

38
00:02:18,473 --> 00:02:19,849
I'm just glad to know
I had an impact.

39
00:02:20,475 --> 00:02:21,893
I meant every word.

40
00:02:22,811 --> 00:02:26,523
In other news, Erin and
Andy are back together.

41
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:29,150
Crazy story.
Yes.

42
00:02:29,234 --> 00:02:32,153
I drove all the way down to
Florida, she was not expecting it,

43
00:02:32,237 --> 00:02:34,072
totally swept her off her feet.
Right? Yeah.

44
00:02:34,239 --> 00:02:35,240
How long
was the drive?

45
00:02:35,490 --> 00:02:36,991
It's like a day and
a half each way.

46
00:02:37,075 --> 00:02:40,453
But when I got there, I went right
up to the house, and I was like...

47
00:02:40,578 --> 00:02:43,498
Day and a half? My lumbar
would be killing me.

48
00:02:43,581 --> 00:02:47,377
You should get this lumbar support
cushion thing my dad has.

49
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:48,753
What's it called?
Um...

50
00:02:49,754 --> 00:02:51,130
Not Easy-Rest.

51
00:02:51,422 --> 00:02:53,341
That gas must've cost
a pretty penny, huh?

52
00:02:53,424 --> 00:02:54,634
Well,
he's got a Prius.

53
00:02:54,759 --> 00:02:56,052
How many times you fill the tank?
Three, four?

54
00:02:56,261 --> 00:02:58,179
What does gas
cost down there?

55
00:02:58,263 --> 00:03:00,348
Lumbar Buddy!
Lumbar Buddy.

56
00:03:00,431 --> 00:03:01,558
Oh, yeah,
Lumbar Buddy.

57
00:03:01,641 --> 00:03:03,476
Tell you what,
I'll email you the story.

58
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,144
It's a real
tearjerker, though.

59
00:03:05,228 --> 00:03:06,771
So read with caution.

60
00:03:07,105 --> 00:03:08,356
Anyway, I know it's
the end of the day.

61
00:03:08,439 --> 00:03:09,816
We just wanted to
stop by and say hi.

62
00:03:09,899 --> 00:03:12,402
And then later on, we have
a reservation at Patsel's.

63
00:03:13,611 --> 00:03:14,779
Miss Lumbar!

64
00:03:15,655 --> 00:03:17,240
Hey, Kev.
Yeah.

65
00:03:17,407 --> 00:03:19,951
Nice sweater.
Thank you!

66
00:03:20,535 --> 00:03:23,121
Nellie was nice enough
to give it to me.

67
00:03:23,705 --> 00:03:26,708
She's sweet. I just
wish there was pockets.

68
00:03:28,501 --> 00:03:30,211
What happened
to Old Salty?

69
00:03:30,295 --> 00:03:31,796
Nellie let me
bobble-ize him.

70
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:34,090
His name is now
Captain Mutato.

71
00:03:35,133 --> 00:03:36,926
I've written quite a bit
of X-Men fan fiction.

72
00:03:37,010 --> 00:03:39,762
Captain Mutato is
half-man, half-mermaid.

73
00:03:39,846 --> 00:03:41,931
So he can fight
crime as a man

74
00:03:42,015 --> 00:03:43,641
and make love
as a mermaid.

75
00:03:44,601 --> 00:03:47,270
Most of my writing
involves the latter.

76
00:03:52,984 --> 00:03:53,985
Okey-doke

77
00:03:56,905 --> 00:03:57,989
Yes?

78
00:04:00,241 --> 00:04:01,242
ANDY; Whoa!

79
00:04:03,328 --> 00:04:06,873
Well, you must be the famous Nellie
Bertram I've been hearing all about.

80
00:04:06,998 --> 00:04:10,543
I am the famous Andy Bernard you
have been hearing all about.

81
00:04:10,668 --> 00:04:12,420
Oh, yes. I just
want to thank you

82
00:04:12,503 --> 00:04:15,423
for jumping in and
minding the store

83
00:04:15,506 --> 00:04:16,883
during my temporary absence.

84
00:04:17,050 --> 00:04:19,260
You are most welcome.

85
00:04:19,469 --> 00:04:22,680
Anyway, now that I'm back, I would
love to have my office back,

86
00:04:22,764 --> 00:04:24,807
whenever you get a chance. No.

87
00:04:25,642 --> 00:04:29,938
Obviously we'll figure
out the logistics

88
00:04:30,021 --> 00:04:32,440
of moving all of this
stuff out of here.

89
00:04:33,107 --> 00:04:36,569
But, you know, the sooner the better.
Get back to normalcy.

90
00:04:36,903 --> 00:04:37,946
Mmm. No.

91
00:04:42,241 --> 00:04:43,242
Thank you.

92
00:04:44,535 --> 00:04:45,536
Okay.

93
00:04:45,620 --> 00:04:46,704
Wait. Uh...

94
00:04:46,955 --> 00:04:49,958
When I showed up here,
there was no manager.

95
00:04:50,041 --> 00:04:52,085
It's like when the Americans
showed up at the Moon.

96
00:04:52,168 --> 00:04:53,461
Nobody was there.

97
00:04:53,544 --> 00:04:55,046
So they planted
their flag,

98
00:04:55,129 --> 00:04:56,756
and it's their
moon now, isn't it?

99
00:04:57,298 --> 00:05:00,927
Nobody likes it, but it's
America's bloody moon.

100
00:05:01,511 --> 00:05:04,347
Just lay him in his crib
and then bicycle his legs.

101
00:05:04,430 --> 00:05:05,682
And then after
Jim quiets down,

102
00:05:05,765 --> 00:05:07,141
you do the same thing
with your baby.

103
00:05:09,143 --> 00:05:10,937
But if he keeps having
problems, just give me a call.

104
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:12,480
Oh, my gosh,
thank you so much.

105
00:05:12,563 --> 00:05:13,773
But seriously, we don't
want to bother you

106
00:05:13,898 --> 00:05:15,066
any more than we already have.
That's it.

107
00:05:15,525 --> 00:05:16,943
It's no bother.
You guys are our friends.

108
00:05:17,318 --> 00:05:19,070
Ravi, our amazing
pediatrician,

109
00:05:19,153 --> 00:05:21,322
was asking us if
we knew any girls,

110
00:05:21,406 --> 00:05:23,950
and I said, "I know
the perfect girl."

111
00:05:24,033 --> 00:05:28,955
Yeah. Because Kelly is Indian and...
Oh, that's it!

112
00:05:30,206 --> 00:05:32,583
Race had nothing
to do with it.

113
00:05:32,667 --> 00:05:34,460
I just knew they'd
be good together.

114
00:05:34,961 --> 00:05:35,962
Why?

115
00:05:36,045 --> 00:05:38,339
Kelly has been
a handful in the past.

116
00:05:38,423 --> 00:05:39,841
But she's had
a bad influence.

117
00:05:39,924 --> 00:05:42,927
She's like an addict, and I
just had to get her clean.

118
00:05:43,886 --> 00:05:44,846
Get lower.

119
00:05:44,929 --> 00:05:47,432
Next, I'm going to set up
my sister with Darryl.

120
00:05:47,515 --> 00:05:48,891
Okay, we get it.

121
00:05:48,933 --> 00:05:51,519
What? I think they'd be good together.
Really?

122
00:05:54,897 --> 00:05:57,692
Um, also, little tip,
never shake the baby.

123
00:05:59,152 --> 00:06:01,279
Sorry, just to be clear, you're
saying do not shake the baby?

124
00:06:01,362 --> 00:06:02,447
Don't shake the baby.

125
00:06:02,530 --> 00:06:04,866
A lot of times parents get frustrated
because the baby's crying,

126
00:06:04,949 --> 00:06:08,911
and they shake the baby,
and you got to...

127
00:06:08,995 --> 00:06:09,996
You can't do that.

128
00:06:10,204 --> 00:06:11,789
Don't shake our baby.
Yeah.

129
00:06:11,873 --> 00:06:13,499
Okay, I'd never
heard that before.

130
00:06:13,624 --> 00:06:14,584
Oh, my God.
So, thank you.

131
00:06:14,667 --> 00:06:16,669
Yeah, I'm glad you said something.
Me, too.

132
00:06:17,545 --> 00:06:19,881
Kelly and I broke up, and she
can do whatever she wants.

133
00:06:19,964 --> 00:06:22,091
And her new boyfriend
seems awesome,

134
00:06:22,175 --> 00:06:24,010
if you're into
Indian people.

135
00:06:24,385 --> 00:06:25,636
I'm not.

136
00:06:27,638 --> 00:06:29,057
And that's
when I realized,

137
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:31,017
if you're gonna put a
thermometer in one end,

138
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:33,311
you'd better put a
lollipop in the other.

139
00:06:33,895 --> 00:06:36,564
Hey, I'm sorry. Is this a
workplace or a Starbucks?

140
00:06:36,647 --> 00:06:39,317
Because I was under the
impression it was a workplace.

141
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:40,735
Maybe I'm
the crazy one.

142
00:06:40,818 --> 00:06:42,987
No. No, we're sorry.
Come on, let's go, Ravi.

143
00:06:43,071 --> 00:06:45,990
Also, since when do we have
guests here without clearance?

144
00:06:46,074 --> 00:06:47,492
I didn't okay this.

145
00:06:49,327 --> 00:06:50,328
Hey, um...

146
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:53,456
What's the deal with this guy?
He's really into Kelly, huh?

147
00:06:54,082 --> 00:06:55,666
Yeah, they're
really great together.

148
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,251
Makes me wonder
if I made a mistake.

149
00:06:57,335 --> 00:07:00,546
No, no, no. Come on. I think you
guys are both happier now, right?

150
00:07:00,630 --> 00:07:03,049
You're single. Plenty of
girls to date, right?

151
00:07:04,342 --> 00:07:05,343
Yeah.

152
00:07:06,052 --> 00:07:08,596
Maybe we weren't right
together, but it's weird,

153
00:07:08,679 --> 00:07:12,266
I'd rather she be alone
than with somebody.

154
00:07:13,184 --> 00:07:14,185
Is that love?

155
00:07:17,021 --> 00:07:18,898
That's about it, yeah.

156
00:07:21,275 --> 00:07:23,319
Well, Nellie picked up
the slack around here

157
00:07:23,402 --> 00:07:26,280
while you were trolling
the Florida beaches for tail

158
00:07:26,364 --> 00:07:28,366
like some college student
on spring break.

159
00:07:29,867 --> 00:07:31,828
I had to tell Erin
how I felt.

160
00:07:31,911 --> 00:07:33,871
Andy, I appreciate
your romantic quest,

161
00:07:33,955 --> 00:07:36,707
and in an age before the
telephone or Internet,

162
00:07:36,874 --> 00:07:39,085
or written language,
that would be compelling.

163
00:07:39,168 --> 00:07:41,629
But there are five, six
devices in this room alone

164
00:07:41,712 --> 00:07:44,382
that would have let you tell her
that without ever going to Florida.

165
00:07:44,465 --> 00:07:47,260
We live in
amazing times.

166
00:07:47,385 --> 00:07:49,428
Yeah, I know
I screwed up.

167
00:07:50,346 --> 00:07:53,141
But I always do
whatever you ask of me,

168
00:07:53,224 --> 00:07:55,518
and this will never
happen again.

169
00:07:55,893 --> 00:07:58,896
And if Erin decides she's made a
mistake and returns to Florida?

170
00:07:59,814 --> 00:08:03,568
At least she knows how I feel,
and I would not follow her.

171
00:08:06,362 --> 00:08:10,366
What if she were kidnapped by a
gang of Albanian human traffickers?

172
00:08:12,243 --> 00:08:13,452
Like in Taken?

173
00:08:13,703 --> 00:08:14,704
What?

174
00:08:15,079 --> 00:08:16,956
Yes, of course,
if she's taken.

175
00:08:17,039 --> 00:08:19,167
That's what I'm talking about.
By Albanians.

176
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:21,335
I would stay
in this office.

177
00:08:22,420 --> 00:08:25,089
Wow, okay. I'll
remember you said that.

178
00:08:31,429 --> 00:08:32,847
Nellie,

179
00:08:34,307 --> 00:08:38,603
you've been terrific
in your interim capacity,

180
00:08:38,728 --> 00:08:41,063
but Andrew is
the rightful manager,

181
00:08:41,147 --> 00:08:43,941
so if you would just
give him his office.

182
00:08:44,108 --> 00:08:45,985
No.
I'm sorry?

183
00:08:47,278 --> 00:08:49,947
This is what I was
trying to tell you.

184
00:08:51,032 --> 00:08:53,451
I'm not accustomed to
people saying no to me.

185
00:08:53,534 --> 00:08:56,495
Well, Bobby,
get accustomed to it,

186
00:08:56,579 --> 00:09:01,959
because then it feels so good
when they finally say yes.

187
00:09:09,091 --> 00:09:11,677
You're both adults.
I'm sure you can

188
00:09:13,679 --> 00:09:16,432
figure this out
between yourselves.

189
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:23,731
I never allow sexual desire to
influence a business decision.

190
00:09:23,814 --> 00:09:28,194
So, I find it best to
recuse myself temporarily

191
00:09:28,277 --> 00:09:29,904
until I've had
a chance to make love,

192
00:09:30,029 --> 00:09:34,742
and then go back and analyze
the situation rationally.

193
00:09:36,827 --> 00:09:39,538
Buffett operates
the same way.

194
00:09:42,291 --> 00:09:44,085
I want to order the zebra
rug for my office,

195
00:09:44,168 --> 00:09:46,170
but can you dye it
entirely black?

196
00:09:48,005 --> 00:09:49,882
No, I still want it
to be a zebra.

197
00:09:51,259 --> 00:09:52,510
Well, I'll know.

198
00:09:53,803 --> 00:09:55,846
Because they're
ridiculous creatures.

199
00:09:56,472 --> 00:09:57,431
They don't know
what they are.

200
00:09:57,515 --> 00:09:59,934
Phyllis says J. Duffy's
might be more our speed.

201
00:10:00,017 --> 00:10:02,853
And if we want even the option
of drawing on the placemats...

202
00:10:05,147 --> 00:10:07,316
I got a little bit
of an anger problem.

203
00:10:08,150 --> 00:10:09,902
Got me in some trouble
a couple years ago.

204
00:10:09,986 --> 00:10:11,696
When I see him
start to get mad,

205
00:10:11,779 --> 00:10:15,324
I just put my hand
on his arm like this.

206
00:10:16,909 --> 00:10:19,829
It reminds me to just
check out and relax.

207
00:10:21,372 --> 00:10:24,875
There's also a lullaby they used to
sing to me when I was growing up.

208
00:10:26,419 --> 00:10:30,339
The state of Pennsylvania
is watching over you

209
00:10:30,756 --> 00:10:34,760
No need for parents,
the governor will do

210
00:10:35,052 --> 00:10:36,304
It's really nice.

211
00:10:37,972 --> 00:10:41,976
The General Assembly's
like a mom and a dad

212
00:10:46,230 --> 00:10:47,440
...had

213
00:10:49,608 --> 00:10:52,361
I got a call
about a trespasser.

214
00:10:52,903 --> 00:10:55,114
Yes. Right this way.

215
00:10:57,491 --> 00:11:01,996
Because they are idiots.
Big, stripy, horsey idiots.

216
00:11:02,079 --> 00:11:04,290
What you don't... Hey!

217
00:11:04,498 --> 00:11:06,834
Hank, please remove
Nellie from my office.

218
00:11:07,126 --> 00:11:08,169
Hank, thank God
you're here.

219
00:11:08,252 --> 00:11:10,588
This psychopath keeps
barging into my office.

220
00:11:10,671 --> 00:11:12,590
It's my office.

221
00:11:13,966 --> 00:11:16,677
Well, she's sitting
there like a manager.

222
00:11:17,762 --> 00:11:19,513
And you're standing
up here like me.

223
00:11:20,556 --> 00:11:23,768
But maybe it's a little
more complicated than that.

224
00:11:30,149 --> 00:11:31,901
I'm going to
count down from five,

225
00:11:31,984 --> 00:11:34,028
and if you're not
out of my office,

226
00:11:34,111 --> 00:11:36,822
I'm going to
dock your pay $100.

227
00:11:37,114 --> 00:11:39,283
Five, four...

228
00:11:39,367 --> 00:11:40,743
You can't dock my pay.

229
00:11:40,826 --> 00:11:42,536
I am your boss.

230
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:44,538
Three, two, one.

231
00:11:44,622 --> 00:11:46,832
Congratulations,
you just lost $100.

232
00:11:47,166 --> 00:11:48,167
Really?

233
00:11:49,126 --> 00:11:53,422
Angela,
dock Andy's pay $100!

234
00:11:53,756 --> 00:11:54,924
On it!

235
00:11:55,549 --> 00:11:59,637
Great! Five, four,
three, two, one.

236
00:12:00,596 --> 00:12:04,809
Angela, please dock
Nellie's pay $100.

237
00:12:08,354 --> 00:12:09,355
Hmm?

238
00:12:09,814 --> 00:12:11,607
Is she responding? Hmm...

239
00:12:12,483 --> 00:12:14,652
Angela? Do you want to go again?

240
00:12:15,111 --> 00:12:16,654
Angela!
Let's go again.

241
00:12:17,279 --> 00:12:19,490
Five, four, three,
two, one.

242
00:12:19,573 --> 00:12:22,701
Oh, she's counting again.
Look out.

243
00:12:22,785 --> 00:12:26,122
- Angela, $200!
- Got it!

